    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe `householdId` is now **deterministic** \u2014 `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`, first 12 hex chars \u2014 so owners sharing a last name and postcode automatically share it, and `sharesHousehold` no longer *creates* the link, it only bypasses the duplicate block.\n\n**`util/HouseholdIdGenerator`** \u2014 now hashes `(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` at 12 chars instead of `(lastName + address)` at 16. Returns `null` when no postcode is on file (an owner with no postcode belongs to no shared household), mirroring the existing postcode-optional handling.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes the deterministic `householdId` for every owner (not just declared members), then applies the new rule: a second owner in an existing household is rejected as a duplicate (409 via the existing `DuplicateIdentityException`) **unless** it declares `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a known member. The old `findOwnersInHousehold`/`joinHousehold`/`isDuplicateIdentity` calls are gone.\n\n**`service/ClinicServiceImpl` + `ClinicService`** \u2014 replaced `isDuplicateIdentity` (identity-key match) with `isHouseholdDuplicate` (any existing owner sharing the computed `householdId`); this subsumes the old identity check since `householdId` is part of the identity key. Removed the now-obsolete `findOwnersInHousehold`/`joinHousehold` and their dead imports. In `saveOwner`, the soft-duplicate detector is skipped for declared members \u2014 *a declared member is not a suspected duplicate*.\n\n**`model/Owner`** \u2014 added a `@Transient declaredHouseholdMember` flag (request-scoped, never persisted) to carry the \"declared member\" signal from controller to the save logic.\n\n**`service/HouseholdMemberCounter`** \u2014 unchanged logic (it already keys off the computed `householdId`, which now drives the household-size input to the membership level); only its javadoc was corrected from \"address\" to \"postcode\".\n\nThe one existing test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
